{title: What A Day That Will Be}
{key: C}

{comment: Chorus}
What a [F]day that will be when my [C]Jesus I shall see
And I [G7]look upon His face
The One [C]who saved me by His grace
When He [F]takes me by the hand
And leads me [C]through the [G/B]Promised [Am]Land
What a [G7]day glorious day that will [C]be

{comment: Verse 1}
[C]There is coming a day when no heartaches shall come
No more [G7]clouds in the sky no more [C]tears to dim the eye
All is [F]peace forevermore on that [C]happy [G/B]golden  [Am]shore
What a [G7]day glorious day that will [C]be

{comment: Verse 2}
[C]There'll be no sorrow there no more burdens to bear
No more [G7]sickness no pain no more [C]parting over there
And for[F]ever I will be with the [C]One who [G/B]died for [Am]me
What a [G7]day glorious day that will [C]be
